  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1024 AM MDT Tue Apr 21 2026\n\nAs a weak shortwave trough comes across today, enough lingering \nmoisture will be present to develop scattered CU this afternoon. \nHudspeth Co will have the best moisture with dew points in the 40s, \nsparking isolated showers and some gusty winds. Otherwise, dry \nconditions and generally light SW winds are forecast today.\n\nThe rest of the forecast period will involve typical spring weather: \ndry and breezy. A large upper low moves into the northern Rockies\non Wed, generating lee troughing along the High Plains. Breezy W\nwinds of about 15-20 mph with gusts to 30-35 mph are expected, a\nbit lighter for far west TX. Storm systems continue to track\nthrough the northern/central Rockies through the weekend, keeping\nwinds at least breezy each afternoon from the W-SW. The dry and\nbreezy conditions day after day will worsen fire danger into the\nweekend as fuels continue to dry. The windiest day of the period\nstill looks to be Sunday with the passage of a shortwave, followed\nby Thursday with gusts to 40 mph. Blowing dust will be a hazard\nthose afternoons.\n\nAfter the slight chance of showers this afternoon out east, rain \nchances will be zero under zonal/SW flow aloft. Temperatures remain \nmild at or slightly above normal into next week.",
